---
mode: agent
setup:
  cwd: '{{workDir}}'
budget:
  timeout: 3m
permissions:
  tools:
    Read: allow
    Glob: allow
    Grep: allow
    Edit: allow
    Write: allow
    Bash: allow
---
You are configuring .gitanalyze.yaml for a git repository.

Read the existing config at {{configPath}}, then analyze this repository to recommend updates:

1. Look at the git log (last 50 commits) to identify bot authors, common noise commit patterns (fixup!, squash!, auto-generated), and low-signal commit types for this repository.
2. Look at the repository structure to identify generated files, lock files, binary or asset files, and IDE/editor config files that should be ignored.
3. If this repo contains Kubernetes manifests, identify auto-generated or low-signal resource types and namespaces.

Edit {{configPath}} directly with your recommendations. Keep the existing filter_sets structure. Add new filter sets if appropriate. Update the includes list. Add YAML comments explaining each addition.

Do NOT remove existing defaults - only add to them. Do NOT add entries that duplicate what's already there. Keep the file concise and well-organized.
